    "narrative": "The **Austin Waves** enter the July 4th slate with a core of high-upside plays, led by **Kyle Tucker** (71.11) and **Cole Carrigg** (71.23). **Cole Carrigg** stands out as our premier play, benefiting significantly from a soft matchup against Robbie Ray and an elite park factor (+14%), which inflates his value against the lefty. Similarly, **Heliot Ramos** (70.57) is a must-start; he faces Sean Sullivan\u2014the weakest starting pitcher on today\u2019s slate with an xERA of 6.43\u2014and benefits from a massive 19% boost due to the favorable pitching profile. **Andy Pages** (69.99) and **Gunnar Henderson** (64.31) round out our top tier, with **Andy Pages** specifically positioned to exploit Wandy Peralta\u2019s lack of deception, providing a solid cushion for our daily efficiency target.\n\nThe most difficult decision for the lineup optimizer involved **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (50.46), who narrowly missed the cut. While his pedigree is elite, the combination of a tough outing against Logan Gilbert and a neutral-to-negative park factor pushed his efficiency score just below the threshold of our starting utility spot, which instead went to the higher-floor profile of **Kyle Tucker**. Meanwhile, our catching duo of **Liam Hicks** (59.93) and **Drake Baldwin** (56.70) remains active, though both are currently subject to \"Lineup Pending\" status; should their actual batting orders drop further down the lineup than our assumed leadoff spots, their efficiency scores will likely see downward pressure.\n\nOwners should remain vigilant regarding weather and official lineup confirmations for our outfield depth. While **Jackson Merrill** (53.21) faces an elite arm in Yoshinobu Yamamoto, his involvement in potential stolen base opportunities keeps his floor respectable. However, **Josh Lowe** (55.20) carries the highest variance today; while his platoon splits against Sonny Gray are favorable, his projected position at the bottom of the order (-6% adjustment) makes him a secondary concern if the rest of the lineup fails to reach base in front of him. We are prioritizing efficiency over raw name value today to navigate the challenging matchups against top-tier arms like Gray and Yamamoto.",
